# Copy this file to .env and fill in the values. install.sh does this for you
# interactively -- this file exists mainly as documentation of every setting.
# chmod 600 .env once filled in (it holds real secrets).

# --- Telegram --------------------------------------------------------------
# Bot token from @BotFather (create a bot with /newbot).
TELEGRAM_BOT_TOKEN=

# Comma-separated numeric Telegram user IDs allowed to use the bot directly
# (in DM, or in a group NOT registered via /registergroup). Get your own ID
# by messaging the bot /chatid once it's running, or via @userinfobot.
# WARNING: leaving this empty makes the bot respond to ANYONE.
ALLOWED_USER_IDS=

# Comma-separated numeric chat IDs (negative numbers) of Telegram groups
# where EVERY member is authorized, no per-person whitelist. Usually left
# empty at install time -- populate it live later via /registergroup (run by
# someone in ALLOWED_USER_IDS, inside the group). See README "Group access".
ALLOWED_GROUP_IDS=

# --- Claude Code -------------------------------------------------------------
# Claude Code signs in to your own Claude Pro/Max subscription directly (that is
# what /start does in Telegram), so NO gateway is needed and these two stay
# empty for a normal install.
#
# Set BOTH only if you deliberately want to route Claude through an
# Anthropic-compatible gateway (9Router, LiteLLM, a local Ollama shim...).
# Leaving either one unset keeps the direct sign-in -- and both are actively
# REMOVED from the CLI's environment in that case, so a value inherited from
# your shell cannot silently redirect traffic somewhere you did not intend.
ANTHROPIC_BASE_URL=
ANTHROPIC_API_KEY=
# Explicit model IDs, never a gateway "combo" alias (a combo hides which model
# actually answered). Bare Anthropic IDs are correct for the direct sign-in;
# behind a gateway they may need that gateway's own provider prefix instead
# (9Router, for one, wants "cc/" -- a bare id 404s there).
CLAUDE_MODEL_PRIMARY=claude-haiku-4-5-20251001
CLAUDE_MODEL_FALLBACK=claude-sonnet-5

# --- agy (Antigravity CLI) --------------------------------------------------
# Leave as default unless you installed agy somewhere non-standard.
AGY_BIN=/home/YOUR_USER/.local/bin/agy
AGY_MODEL_PRIMARY=gemini-3.7-flash-medium
AGY_MODEL_FALLBACK=gemini-3.1-pro-low

# --- Tuning (optional, defaults are usually fine) ---------------------------
# ALLOWED_TOOLS=Bash,WebSearch,WebFetch
# CLAUDE_TIMEOUT_SECONDS=600
# AGY_TIMEOUT_SECONDS=300
# AGY_PRINT_TIMEOUT=280s
# CLAUDE_BIN=claude
# RCLONE_BIN=rclone

# --- The fallback chain -----------------------------------------------------
# Which providers are used, in what order, and what each is called, all from one
# setting: provider:model:label, tried left to right. This is what /providers
# displays and what every reply's "-- by <label>" tag comes from. Unset means the
# 4-tier default below, built from the model settings above.
# TIERS=agy:gemini-3.7-flash-medium:mini,agy:gemini-3.1-pro-low:mini pro,claude:claude-haiku-4-5-20251001:dede iku,claude:claude-sonnet-5:dede nnet
#
# Two extra tiers (Claude Opus, Gemini Pro-high) are defined in code and sit
# OUTSIDE this chain on purpose -- they are reachable only by asking for one by
# name with /usemodel, never by automatic fallback, so a routine turn can never
# escalate itself into the expensive tier. Nothing to configure here.

# --- Write mode (see README "Write mode") -----------------------------------
# The two-key setup: agent_active is a symlink /unlock flips between them.
# SSH_ACTIVE_KEY=~/.ssh/agent_active
# SSH_RO_KEY=~/.ssh/agent_readonly
# SSH_RW_KEY=~/.ssh/agent_write
#
# How long /unlock opens write mode for. A window opened from a GROUP is capped
# tighter than one from a DM: /unlock hands out open-ended write access for the
# whole window rather than approving one visible action, so a group gets a
# shorter leash regardless of what it asks for.
# WRITE_MODE_DEFAULT_MINUTES=15
# WRITE_MODE_MAX_MINUTES=60
# WRITE_MODE_GROUP_MAX_MINUTES=10

# --- Language ---------------------------------------------------------------
# Language for the bot's OWN fixed text (command replies, wizards, PIN keypad)
# in a chat that has not picked one with /lang yet. "id" or "en".
# This does NOT affect the agent's actual answers -- being an LLM, those already
# mirror whatever language you write your prompt in. /help has its own separate
# EN/ID picker, unaffected by this.
# DEFAULT_LANGUAGE=id

# --- Google Drive (optional, see README "Google Drive") ---------------------
# Root folder every upload lands under, inside whichever connected account the
# chat is using. Accounts themselves are rclone remotes named "gdrive" or
# "gdrive_<something>" -- that naming convention IS the registry, nothing to set
# here. In a group, uploads go into a per-group subfolder under this root.
# GDRIVE_ROOT=iSmart-LA Data
